  "worked_solution": "Since the tangent of an angle equals the cotangent of its complement, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{51}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡({90}^{∘}-{51}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cot}⁡{39}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={39}^{∘}$ satisfies the given equation.",
